notes.body:
@Lekensteyn I think I finished the functional part, so now I'll clean up the code and I'll be done.
The sftp dissector is now in its own file, so that is easily separated.
On the other hand, reassembly is pretty tightly spun with the decryption (if a cipher block spans two TCP packets, you cannot decrypt it before you have a complete block, plus you need to decrypt a block in quite a few algorithms to get the block size), so I don't know to what extent it is meaningful to separate it... That being said, reassembly has only been implemented for cbc and ctr algos, I'm waiting for your opinion before I finish gcm and chacha.

Only keep it if you ever expect it to be helpful, and do clean it up. Lots of code use something like:
```
//#define DEBUG_SSH_DECRYPTION

#ifdef DEBUG_SSH_DECRYPTION
    g_debug("...");
#endif
```
but an alternative that could also work is:
```
    if (DEBUG_SSH_DECRYPTION) {
        g_debug("...");
    }
```
The benefit of the latter is compile-time checking. If the macro is not defined, then the code should be optimized away.

@jmayer2 I have been waiting for your message for a very long time!
Please help me to fix my patches so they can be merged.
Thank you.

